--- ARTIFACT NOTES ---
Surface files (src/main/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/StatusHero):
  StatusHero.kt      (view: stateful entry + stateless renderer; status ring/glyph; merged polite status
                      region; subline + inline Live label; refresh CTA via shared Button; authored status
                      glyph set; previews; one-shot PII-safe view.opened),
  StatusHeroModel.kt (pure port of the web STATUS_CONFIG -> HeroStatus enum + StatusTone/StatusGlyphKind +
                      projectStatus projection + StatusHeroCta + view.opened diagnostics; SLUG=StatusHero).
  Web source (web/src/components/status/StatusHero.tsx) is a pure presentational hero (no data hook, no
  useTranslation) -> no P1/S8 Source/ViewModel (sibling ScoreBadge/BatteryDelta/ProgressRing precedent).
  The web spec has no fetch, so no loading/error/stale/offline lifecycle is invented (honesty covenant: no
  scope narrowing, no silent drift). Reproduced states: the five status branches healthy/degraded/unhealthy/
  unknown/maintenance (unknown = the cold-start / not-yet-known surface, always a non-blank card), plus the
  headline-override, subline, inline live-dot, and CTA branches.

Token mapping (web STATUS_CONFIG colour family -> P1/S9 token):
  healthy green -> status.success; degraded amber -> status.warning; unhealthy red -> status.danger;
  maintenance blue -> status.info; unknown zinc -> onSurfaceVariant (muted). The web glow
  (boxShadow 0 0 60px rgba) -> the GlassPanel tinted `accent` border (the platform glow replacement the shared
  GlassPanel documents): Success/Warning/Danger/Info, and None for the neutral unknown tier.
  Glyphs (web lucide -> authored 24x24 stroked vectors, same style as DataDisplayGlyphs/FeedbackGlyphs):
  CheckCircle/AlertTriangle/XCircle/HelpCircle/Wrench; the CTA reuses FeedbackGlyphs.Refresh. XCircle and
  HelpCircle are in no shared catalog, so the full status set is authored locally (per-surface glyph precedent).

i18n (P1/S10): the web component HARDCODES its default headlines (it has no useTranslation; the prompt extracted
  zero keys -- "surface is anonymous"). The native covenant forbids English literals, so each default headline
  is resolved through EXISTING canonical catalog keys rather than inventing keys the web app does not use:
  healthy->translation_Healthy, degraded->translation_Degraded, unhealthy->translation_Unhealthy,
  unknown->translation_Unknown, maintenance->translation_serviceMode_banner_maintenanceTitle ("Scheduled
  maintenance", the exact web string); the inline live label->translation_Live. No strings.xml/en.json change is
  needed or made. The primary call path (web SystemStatusPage) supplies an explicit localized headline anyway.
  web `id` (StickyCompactHero IntersectionObserver anchor) has no DOM analogue on native and is not ported;
  `className` -> Modifier.

Unit tests (run by the gate, :android:testReleaseUnitTest): StatusHeroModelTest=8, StatusHeroDiagnosticsTest=3
  -> 11 tests, 0 failures (full module suite: 14834 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors across 1147 suites). They cover
  the per-status tone+glyph projection, completeness/distinctness of the five tiers, the CTA defaults, and the
  PII-safe view.opened (Info level, surface=StatusHero, no status payload / no digits).

UI test (src/androidTest/.../statushero/StatusHeroUiTest.kt): per-status localized default headline, headline
  override, subline, inline Live label (via the stateless content + slot, no DataContainer), CTA click handler,
  the polite status live region (a11y), and the one-shot view.opened. It executes under
  :android:connectedAndroidTest on a device/emulator (none on this runner), the same split the sibling
  ScoreBadge/BatteryDelta UiTests document. NOTE: the androidTest source set as a whole does not compile on this
  runner -- PRE-EXISTING sibling files (dashboard/widgets/*, modals-dialogs/*, feature-views/*, and sibling
  sharedsurfaces/* incl. the untouched ScoreBadgeUiTest) reference unresolved androidx.compose.ui.test symbols
  (assertExists/assertDoesNotExist/onAllNodes/assert); 55 such diagnostics, none in StatusHeroUiTest.
  StatusHeroUiTest itself introduces no compile error (verified absent from the
  :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin diagnostic inventory) and passes ktlintAndroidTestSourceSetCheck. This
  is independent of StatusHero and outside the four gate steps (which build main + run JVM unit tests, not
  instrumented compilation).

Capability: Java 17 target (JDK 21 toolchain), Kotlin 2.4.0 (>= the prompt's 2.2.x floor; ADR-012 lock), Compose
